  "docs" : [
    {
      "source" : "Northpine Help Center, Cards",
      "text" : "# Issue a card to someone\n\nOpen Cards and press Issue card. Choose the cardholder and whether the card is virtual or physical, give it a name, then set its limit and how often the limit resets. A physical card also asks where to post it. Review the details, tick that the cardholder has read the card policy, and press Issue card.",
      "title" : "Issue a card to someone"
    },
    {
      "source" : "Northpine Help Center, Cards",
      "text" : "# Freeze or unfreeze a card\n\nOpen Cards, choose the card and press Freeze under the table, or open the card and turn on Freeze this card. A frozen card declines every purchase until it is unfrozen. Nothing else about it changes.",
      "title" : "Freeze or unfreeze a card"
    },
    {
      "source" : "Northpine Help Center, Cards",
      "text" : "# Change a card's limit\n\nOpen the card from Cards. Under Spending limit, drag the slider or use the stepper beside it, and choose how often the limit resets. Press Save changes.",
      "title" : "Change a card's limit"
    },
    {
      "source" : "Northpine Help Center, Expenses",
      "text" : "# Split an expense across categories\n\nOpen the expense from Expenses and press Split. Give each part a category and an amount. The parts must add up to the whole before Save split can be pressed. Split evenly shares the amount between the parts.",
      "title" : "Split an expense across categories"
    },
    {
      "source" : "Northpine Help Center, Expenses",
      "text" : "# Find purchases with no receipt\n\nOpen Expenses and tick Missing receipt only. Select the purchases, open Actions and choose Request Receipts to remind their owners.",
      "title" : "Find purchases with no receipt"
    },
    {
      "source" : "Northpine Help Center, Reimbursements",
      "text" : "# Ask to be paid back\n\nOpen Reimbursements and press New request. Give the request a title, add a line for each thing you paid for with its date and amount, choose where to be paid, and press Submit request.",
      "title" : "Ask to be paid back"
    },
    {
      "source" : "Northpine Help Center, Approvals",
      "text" : "# Approve or reject a request\n\nOpen Approvals and choose a request from the list. Press Approve, or Reject and give a reason the requester will see. Requests over $5,000 go on to Finance after you.",
      "title" : "Approve or reject a request"
    },
    {
      "source" : "Northpine Help Center, Approvals",
      "text" : "# Hand your approvals to someone while you are away\n\nOpen Approvals and press Delegate. Choose who covers for you and until when, then press Start delegating.",
      "title" : "Hand your approvals to someone while you are away"
    },
    {
      "source" : "Northpine Help Center, Bills",
      "text" : "# Pay a bill\n\nOpen Bills and stay on To pay. Choose the bill and press Pay bill. Choose how to pay, which account to pay from and when, then confirm. A bill from a vendor on hold cannot be paid until the hold is lifted in Vendors.",
      "title" : "Pay a bill"
    },
    {
      "source" : "Northpine Help Center, Vendors",
      "text" : "# Hold or release payments to a vendor\n\nOpen Vendors and choose the vendor. On the Details tab, turn Hold payments to this vendor on or off. While it is on, none of the vendor's bills can be paid.",
      "title" : "Hold or release payments to a vendor"
    },
    {
      "source" : "Northpine Help Center, Budgets",
      "text" : "# Change a budget\n\nOpen Budgets and press Edit beside the budget. Use the stepper for each line to raise or lower it, choose when the owner is warned, and press Save budget.",
      "title" : "Change a budget"
    },
    {
      "source" : "Northpine Help Center, Accounting",
      "text" : "# Choose which account a category is booked to\n\nOpen Accounting and choose Mappings. Each category has a pop-up with the account it is booked to. Change it and press Save mappings. Tick Apply to past purchases too to rebook what was already spent.",
      "title" : "Choose which account a category is booked to"
    },
    {
      "source" : "Northpine Help Center, Accounting",
      "text" : "# Close the books for a month\n\nOpen Accounting and choose Month-end close. Work down the checklist: each check that is not done has a button that takes you to where it is fixed. When all six are ticked, press Close for the month and confirm.",
      "title" : "Close the books for a month"
    },
    {
      "source" : "Northpine Help Center, People",
      "text" : "# Invite people to Northpine\n\nOpen People and press Invite people. Type their email addresses, choose a role and a department, and press Send invites. They show as Invited until they accept.",
      "title" : "Invite people to Northpine"
    },
    {
      "source" : "Northpine Help Center, People",
      "text" : "# Change what a role may do\n\nOpen People and choose Roles and permissions. Tick or untick an ability under a role, then press Save permissions. Admins may always do everything.",
      "title" : "Change what a role may do"
    },
    {
      "source" : "Northpine Help Center, Policies",
      "text" : "# Change a spending rule\n\nOpen Policies. Switch a rule on or off, or press Change amount beside it. Nothing takes effect until you press Publish at the top of the screen.",
      "title" : "Change a spending rule"
    },
    {
      "source" : "Northpine Help Center, Reports",
      "text" : "# Export a report\n\nOpen Reports, choose how to group the spend and the dates, then open Export and choose a spreadsheet or a document. The same exports are in the File menu, under Export.",
      "title" : "Export a report"
    }
  ],
  "id" : "site_northpine_mac",
  "learn" : false,
  "name" : "Northpine",
  "notes" : "Northpine is a Mac app, not a website. Companies use it to manage what they spend: company cards, expenses, reimbursements, approvals, bills and vendors, budgets, and the accounting behind them.\n\n- A \"path\" here is a screen of the app. The sidebar on the left switches screens. It has five groups: Overview (Home, Inbox), Spend (Cards, Expenses, Reimbursements), Payables (Approvals, Bills, Vendors), Finance (Budgets, Accounting, Reports) and Company (People, Policies, Help Center).\n- Every screen is also in the Go menu in the menu bar, and in the command palette (the Command palette button in the toolbar).\n- Menu bar items are listed as elements too. One marked \"in the closed File menu\" is reached by opening that menu first. Point at the item itself: the app moves the pointer to the menu's title until the menu is open.\n- Exports are in the File menu under Export. Report exports are one menu deeper, under File, Export, Reports.\n- Settings is a separate window, opened with Settings… in the Northpine menu or in the account menu in the toolbar. It has five panes along its top: General, Notifications, Security, Plan and billing, Integrations. API keys and two-factor authentication are on Security.\n- Accounting has four sections chosen by a row of segments: Chart of accounts, Mappings, Sync and Month-end close.\n- Tables (Cards, Expenses, Bills, People) work the same way: click a row to choose it, then use the buttons under the table, like Open card or Pay bill. Those buttons are off until a row is chosen.\n- Approvals, Vendors, Inbox and Help Center show a list on the left and what was chosen on the right.\n- A bill cannot be paid while its vendor is on hold. The hold is the \"Hold payments to this vendor\" checkbox on the vendor's Details tab in Vendors.\n- Changes to Policies do nothing until Publish at the top of that screen is pressed.\n- What someone can see depends on their role and the company's plan. If a screen is missing from the sidebar, say that their role or plan does not include it. Do not send them looking for it.",
